 rethrowing?","options":["Turn the error into success","Just delete the payload","Restart the app to clear the error state","Log the error or clean up resources"],"explanation":"Logging and compensation."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ámbitos o componentes ayudan a gestionar fallos transitorios? (Elige 2)","options":["Logger","Set Variable","Until Successful","Choice","Estrategia de reconexión del conector"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Reintentos y reconexión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two scopes/components help handle transient failures? (Choose 2)","options":["Logger","Set Variable","Until Successful","Choice","Connector reconnection strategy"],"explanation":"Retries and reconnection."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué expresión filtra un On Error por el código HTTP devuelto por un servicio remoto?","options":["type=\"404\"","when=\"${statusCode}\"","type=\"HTTP:404\"","when=\"#[error.muleMessage.attributes.statusCode == 404]\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se puede inspeccionar el mensaje del error.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which expression filters an On Error by the remote HTTP status?","options":["type=\"404\"","when=\"${statusCode}\"","type=\"HTTP:404\"","when=\"#[error.muleMessage.attributes.statusCode == 404]\""],"explanation":"The error's message can be inspected."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error de APIkit se suele mapear a 405?","options":["APIKIT:NOT_ACCEPTABLE","APIKIT:BAD_REQUEST","APIKIT:NOT_FOUND","APIKIT:METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Method not allowed.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which APIkit error is usually mapped to 405?","options":["APIKIT:NOT_ACCEPTABLE","APIKIT:BAD_REQUEST","APIKIT:NOT_FOUND","APIKIT:METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED"],"explanation":"Method not allowed."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para no exponer detalles internos en errores 500?","options":["Devolver error.description completo siempre","Devolver el XML de configuración","Devolver la traza de Java","Devolver un mensaje genérico y registrar el detalle internamente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Seguridad de la información.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What avoids exposing internals in 500 errors?","options":["Always return the full error.description","Return the config XML","Return the Java stack trace","Return a generic message and log details internally"],"explanation":"Information security."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error lanza Raise Error si se define type=\"APP:INVALID_ORDER\"?","options":["VALIDATION:INVALID_ORDER","APP:INVALID_ORDER","HTTP:BAD_REQUEST","MULE:ANY"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Namespace propio de la app.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which error does Raise Error throw with type=\"APP:INVALID_ORDER\"?","options":["VALIDATION:INVALID_ORDER","APP:INVALID_ORDER","HTTP:BAD_REQUEST","MULE:ANY"],"explanation":"An app-specific namespace."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con las transacciones si se produce un error en un Try transaccional con On Error Propagate?","options":["Se revierte la transacción","Se duplica","Se ignora","Se confirma la transacción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Propagate provoca rollback.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to transactions if a transactional Try errors with On Error Propagate?","options":["The transaction rolls back","It duplicates","It's ignored","The transaction commits"],"explanation":"Propagate triggers rollback."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con la transacción en un Try transaccional con On Error Continue?","options":["Se reintenta","Se confirma (commit)","Se pausa","Se revierte"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Continue se trata como éxito.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to the transaction in a transactional Try with On Error Continue?","options":["It retries","It commits","It pauses","It rolls back"],"explanation":"Continue counts as success."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos jerarquías de tipos de error son ciertas? (Elige 2)","options":["MULE:EXPRESSION incluye a ANY","ANY incluye a todos los tipos","DB incluye a APIKIT","VALIDATION incluye a HTTP","HTTP:NOT_FOUND es un tipo de error HTTP"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"ANY es la raíz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two error type hierarchies are true? (Choose 2)","options":["MULE:EXPRESSION includes ANY","ANY includes all types","DB includes APIKIT","VALIDATION includes HTTP","HTTP:NOT_FOUND is an HTTP error type"],"explanation":"ANY is the root."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para tratar de forma distinta errores de conexión y de validación en el mismo flujo?","options":["Ignorar los de validación","Usar Round Robin","Varios On Error con tipos distintos","Un único On Error ANY con un Choice dentro obligatoriamente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Handlers específicos por tipo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How to treat connection and validation errors differently in one flow?","options":["Ignore validation ones","Use Round Robin","Several On Errors with different types","Mandatorily one On Error ANY with a Choice inside"],"explanation":"Type-specific handlers."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un error se produce dentro de un On Error?","options":["Se ejecuta el siguiente On Error","Se reintenta el On Error","Se propaga el nuevo error","Se ignora"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los errores en handlers se propagan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if an error occurs inside an On Error?","options":["The next On Error runs","The On Error retries","The new error propagates","It's ignored"],"explanation":"Errors in handlers propagate."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica error.description?","options":["El payload","El tipo del error","El texto descriptivo del error","El nombre del flujo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Mensaje legible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does error.description hold?","options":["The payload","The error type","The error's descriptive text","The flow name"],"explanation":"A readable message."}}},{"domain":"D8","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve payload groupBy $.country sobre un array de clientes?","options":["Un array ordenado alfabéticamente por el nombre del país de cada cliente","El número de clientes distintos que hay en cada país de la lista","Un array de arrays con un cliente en cada posición","Un objeto cuyas claves son países"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"groupBy devuelve objeto clave → array.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does payload groupBy $.country return on a customer array?","options":["An array sorted alphabetically by each customer's country name","The number of distinct customers per country in the list","An array of arrays with one customer each","An object keyed by country"],"explanation":"groupBy returns key → array object."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que una API rechace pedidos con cantidad negativa antes de procesarlos?","options":["Un Round Robin entre dos implementaciones del flujo","Un validador al inicio del flujo","Un Scatter-Gather que envíe el pedido a todos los sistemas a la vez","Un Logger que registre la cantidad negativa y continúe con el proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Validación temprana.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What makes an API reject orders with negative quantity before processing?","options":["A Round Robin between two flow implementations","A validator at flow start","A Scatter-Gather sending the order to every system at once","A Logger recording the negative quantity and continuing"],"explanation":"Early validation."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué router conviene para llamar a un CRM y a un ERP a la vez y devolver ambos datos combinados?","options":["Round Robin, que alterna entre CRM y ERP en cada petición","Scatter-Gather","First Successful, que llama a ambos y combina las respuestas","Choice, que ejecuta todas las rutas cuya condición se cumple a la vez"],"correct":[1],"explanati